Enforcee — Licence
==================

Copyright (c) 2026 Enforcee. All rights reserved.

This software is **source-available**, not open source. It is published so that
it can be read, run and verified. It is not published so that it can be reused.


Why you can read this at all
-----------------------------

Enforcee tells you whether an AI followed your rules, and it installs a component
that runs inside your development environment with access to your files. A tool
like that asking you to trust an unreadable binary has not earned the trust it is
asking for.

So every line is here. Read it, run it, check that it does what the marketing
says, and satisfy yourself that the `audit`, `health`, `learn` and `session`
commands make no network calls — because they do not, and you should not have to
take our word for that either.


What you may do
---------------

- **Use it.** Run the software, on any machine, for any purpose including
  commercial work, subject to the Terms of Service at
  https://enforcee.vercel.app/terms.
- **Read all of it**, and audit it however you like.
- **Run modified copies locally** for your own debugging, security review, or to
  satisfy yourself about its behaviour.
- **Quote short excerpts** when discussing, reviewing, teaching or criticising it,
  with attribution.
- **Report bugs and vulnerabilities.** These are genuinely welcome.


What you may not do
-------------------

Without prior written permission, you may not:

- copy, redistribute, republish, sublicense or sell this software or any part of
  it, in source or compiled form;
- create or distribute derivative works, forks, or ports;
- remove or alter this notice, the copyright notices, or any licence check;
- use this software, or the methodology, rule taxonomy, evaluation prompts,
  thresholds, scoring, or receipt format it contains, to build, train or improve
  a competing product;
- use it to provide a competing service to third parties.

The licence enforcement mechanism is a signed token verified offline. Nothing
about that is obscured, and circumventing it is a breach of these terms rather
than a puzzle to solve. If you need access and cannot pay, ask — see below.


Third-party components
